WEBVTT

00:29:58.621 --> 00:30:02.663
Another way, Emily measured individualism
was by looking at Social Security data

00:30:02.954 --> 00:30:06.996
to see what parents name their kids during
good and bad economic times.

00:30:07.954 --> 00:30:10.121
Emily found that when the
economy is doing well,

00:30:10.454 --> 00:30:15.163
parents are more likely to give their kids
unique names. I'm looking at you.

00:30:15.204 --> 00:30:17.913
Blue Ivy, when the economy is struggling,

00:30:18.038 --> 00:30:20.746
parents choose from a smaller
set of more common names,

00:30:21.079 --> 00:30:22.746
which are often biblical names.

00:30:23.246 --> 00:30:29.496
It used to be in the 1950s when
out of 15 boys would receive

00:30:29.496 --> 00:30:33.996
the most common name. Fast
forward to 2013.